1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,136
这是一个医院数据库，每个病人一条记录
Here is a hospital database, one row per patient.

2
00:00:03,456 --> 00:00:08,043
有位研究者问了个看似无害的问题：有多少病人患有疾病 X？
A researcher asks an innocent question: how many patients have condition X?

3
00:00:08,363 --> 00:00:10,411
医院不公开任何记录
The hospital releases no records.

4
00:00:10,731 --> 00:00:12,331
它只给了一个数：41
It just says: 41.

5
00:00:12,567 --> 00:00:15,490
一周后，一位新病人 Alice 入院了
A week later, one new patient, Alice, is admitted.

6
00:00:15,810 --> 00:00:17,410
研究者又问了一遍
The researcher asks again.

7
00:00:17,602 --> 00:00:19,287
现在答案是 42
The answer is now 42.

8
00:00:19,533 --> 00:00:23,761
两数一减，研究者就知道了 Alice 一件很具体的事
Subtract, and the researcher has learned something very specific about Alice,

9
00:00:23,761 --> 00:00:25,464
却一条记录都没看
without seeing a single record.

10
00:00:25,784 --> 00:00:28,173
继续之前，先自己试着补上这个漏洞
Before we go on, try to fix this yourself.

11
00:00:28,493 --> 00:00:32,717
暂停想一想：人数四舍五入到十位，能保护 Alice 吗？
Pause and ponder: would rounding the count to the nearest ten protect Alice?

12
00:00:33,037 --> 00:00:35,064
需要多想一会儿的话，可以先暂停视频
Pause the video if you need more time.

13
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:46,743
大多数星期里，确实可以
Most weeks, yes.

14
00:00:46,793 --> 00:00:49,537
但如果人数从 44 变成 45
But if the count goes from 44 to 45,

15
00:00:49,537 --> 00:00:54,644
取整后的答案就从 40 跳到 50，Alice 又暴露了
the rounded answer jumps from 40 to 50, and Alice is exposed again.

16
00:00:54,964 --> 00:00:59,231
任何确定性的规则，只要答案会变，就一定在某处有这样的跳变
Any fixed rule that ever changes its answer has a jump like that somewhere.

17
00:00:59,467 --> 00:01:02,710
那发布统计量，到底怎样才算不泄露隐私？
So what would it even mean for a statistic to be private?

18
00:01:03,030 --> 00:01:05,909
如果靠加噪声，那加多少才够？
And if the fix is to add noise, how much is enough?

19
00:01:06,150 --> 00:01:08,949
2006 年，Cynthia Dwork、Frank McSherry
In 2006, Cynthia Dwork, Frank McSherry,

20
00:01:08,949 --> 00:01:10,887
Kobbi Nissim 和 Adam Smith
Kobbi Nissim and Adam Smith

21
00:01:10,887 --> 00:01:14,906
用这篇 paper 回答了这两个问题：《Calibrating Noise to
answered both questions in this paper: Calibrating Noise

22
00:01:14,906 --> 00:01:17,777
Sensitivity in Private Data Analysis》
to Sensitivity in Private Data Analysis.

23
00:01:18,097 --> 00:01:21,644
它开创了我们今天所说的差分隐私
It founded what we now call differential privacy,

24
00:01:21,644 --> 00:01:24,177
differential privacy，2017 年还获得了哥德尔奖
and in 2017 it won the Gödel Prize.

25
00:01:24,417 --> 00:01:28,499
这期讲三个核心想法：隐私的定义；一个数，叫敏感度
This video covers its three big ideas: a definition of privacy,

26
00:01:28,499 --> 00:01:33,100
sensitivity；以及一个公式，算噪声加多少才够
a number called sensitivity, and a recipe for how much noise is enough.

27
00:01:33,420 --> 00:01:37,106
还有个出人意料的限制：要按这个定义不泄露隐私
Plus a surprising limit on what one published table can achieve,

28
00:01:37,106 --> 00:01:39,179
一张公开的表能做的有限
if it must be private in this sense.

29
00:01:40,617 --> 00:01:42,921
先画一张地图，看看这篇 paper 从哪儿来
First, a map of where this paper comes from.

30
00:01:43,241 --> 00:01:49,278
1965 年，Stanley Warner 为敏感问题调查提出了随机响应
In 1965, Stanley Warner proposed randomized response for sensitive surveys.

31
00:01:49,598 --> 00:01:52,329
在常见的版本里，你私下掷一枚硬币
In a popular version, you flip a coin in private.

32
00:01:52,649 --> 00:01:54,249
正面，你就如实回答
Heads, you answer truthfully.

33
00:01:54,526 --> 00:01:58,003
反面，你就再掷一次：正面答“是”，反面答“否”
Tails, you flip again and say yes for heads, no for tails.

34
00:01:58,323 --> 00:02:00,612
任何一个“是”，都可能只是硬币说的
Any single yes could be the coin talking,

35
00:02:00,612 --> 00:02:04,297
但问上成千上万人，真实比例照样能估出来
yet over thousands of people the true rate can still be estimated.

36
00:02:04,617 --> 00:02:06,200
记住这枚硬币
Keep this coin in mind.

37
00:02:06,250 --> 00:02:11,588
之后几十年，统计学家和计算机科学家，不断改进这类 trick
Over the following decades, statisticians and computer scientists refined such tricks,

38
00:02:11,588 --> 00:02:16,554
分成两种思路：要么扰动输入的数据，要么扰动输出的答案
in two flavours: scramble the data going in, or scramble the answers coming out.

39
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:20,576
与此同时，最容易想到的办法，也就是直接去掉姓名，却一再失败
Meanwhile, the obvious fix, just remove the names, kept failing.

40
00:02:20,896 --> 00:02:24,341
Latanya Sweeney 发现，光凭邮编
Latanya Sweeney showed that ZIP code, birth date

41
00:02:24,341 --> 00:02:28,361
出生日期和性别，就能唯一识别大多数美国人
and sex alone single out most Americans, and in 1997 she

42
00:02:28,361 --> 00:02:33,889
1997 年，她把号称匿名的病历和公开的选民名单一对照
linked supposedly anonymous hospital records to a public voter list and found

43
00:02:33,889 --> 00:02:36,042
就认出了马萨诸塞州州长
the governor of Massachusetts.

44
00:02:36,362 --> 00:02:39,670
教训是：隐私必须是发布过程的性质
The lesson: privacy must be a property of the process,

45
00:02:39,670 --> 00:02:41,876
而不在于发布出来的表看起来怎么样
not of how the released table looks,

46
00:02:41,876 --> 00:02:44,939
而且无论攻击者还知道什么，它都必须成立
and it must hold whatever else the attacker knows.

47
00:02:45,184 --> 00:02:46,185
然后在 2003 年
Then, in 2003,

48
00:02:46,185 --> 00:02:50,048
Irit Dinur 和 Kobbi Nissim 证明了一个令人警醒的结论
Irit Dinur and Kobbi Nissim proved something sobering.

49
00:02:50,368 --> 00:02:55,226
问题答得太多、太准，误差远小于根号 n
Answer too many questions too accurately, with errors much smaller than the square

50
00:02:55,226 --> 00:02:59,136
攻击者就能重构出几乎整个数据库
root of n, and an attacker can rebuild almost the entire database.

51
00:02:59,456 --> 00:03:02,826
我们那个做减法的攻击，其实就是这种攻击只问两个问题的版本
Our subtraction was the two-question version of this attack.

52
00:03:03,146 --> 00:03:05,685
噪声，就是回答很多问题的代价
Noise is the price of answering many questions.

53
00:03:05,934 --> 00:03:10,734
反过来也有好消息：问题数量有限，适量噪声就够了
The hopeful flip side: with a limited number of questions, modest noise is enough.

54
00:03:11,054 --> 00:03:15,253
Dwork、Nissim 和合作者据此做了个叫 SuLQ 的框架
Dwork, Nissim and colleagues built this into a framework called SuLQ,

55
00:03:15,253 --> 00:03:16,653
意思是只问次线性数量的 query（查询）
for sub-linear queries,

56
00:03:16,653 --> 00:03:18,904
它回答带噪声的求和，比如人数
which answers noisy sums like counts.

57
00:03:19,224 --> 00:03:20,974
记住这个上限
Remember that limit on questions.

58
00:03:21,294 --> 00:03:23,192
这篇 paper 把它变成了一笔预算
This paper turns it into a budget.

59
00:03:23,434 --> 00:03:25,188
但 SuLQ 只能处理求和
But SuLQ only covered sums,

60
00:03:25,188 --> 00:03:29,023
而且它的定义容许以极小的概率发生大量泄露
and its definition tolerated a tiny chance of a large leak.

61
00:03:29,343 --> 00:03:32,466
这篇 paper 迈出了一大步：数据的任意函数
This paper takes the leap: any function of the data,

62
00:03:32,466 --> 00:03:35,828
一个干净的定义和一条简单的噪声规则
one clean definition, and one simple rule for the noise.

63
00:03:36,148 --> 00:03:40,096
很应景的是，它发表在密码学会议上，那里的习惯是先定义安全性
Fittingly, it appeared at a cryptography conference, where the habit

64
00:03:40,096 --> 00:03:44,682
要求能抵御所有可能的攻击者，再去证明
is to define security against every possible attacker first, and then prove it.

65
00:03:47,033 --> 00:03:48,434
先交代一下 setting
Here is the setting.

66
00:03:48,484 --> 00:03:50,588
可信的服务器，也就是数据管理者
A trusted server, the curator,

67
00:03:50,588 --> 00:03:53,604
持有数据库 x：n 条记录，每人一条
holds a database x: n rows, one per person.

68
00:03:53,924 --> 00:03:55,589
分析者发来 query f
An analyst sends a query f,

69
00:03:55,589 --> 00:04:00,089
数据库的任意函数，返回一个数或一列数
any function of the database that returns a number, or a list of numbers.

70
00:04:00,333 --> 00:04:03,747
数据管理者从不公开真实答案 f(x)
The curator never releases the honest answer, f(x).

71
00:04:04,067 --> 00:04:08,675
它的做法是先抽一个随机噪声 Y，再公开 f(x) 加 Y
Instead it draws random noise, Y, and releases f(x) + Y.

72
00:04:08,995 --> 00:04:13,048
因为分析者可以一直问下去，所以这叫交互式的 setting
Because the analyst can keep asking, this is called the interactive setting.

73
00:04:13,368 --> 00:04:17,462
另一种做法是发布一张经过隐私处理的表
The alternative, publishing one sanitized table and walking away,

74
00:04:17,462 --> 00:04:18,929
然后撒手不管，这叫非交互式
is non-interactive.

75
00:04:18,979 --> 00:04:22,840
原文最后证明了，前者从根本上更强大
At the end, the paper proves the first is fundamentally more powerful.

76
00:04:23,083 --> 00:04:27,521
所以一切都归结到一个问题：Y 应该服从什么分布？
So everything hinges on one question: what distribution should Y have?

77
00:04:27,841 --> 00:04:30,166
噪声太少，Alice 就暴露了
Too little noise, and Alice is exposed.

78
00:04:30,486 --> 00:04:32,449
太多，答案就没用了
Too much, and the answer is useless.

79
00:04:32,769 --> 00:04:36,673
标题已经给出了答案：按敏感度校准噪声
The title gives the answer: calibrate the noise to the sensitivity.

80
00:04:36,993 --> 00:04:39,382
不过我们先要搞清楚：到底什么叫不泄露隐私？
But first, what does private actually mean?

81
00:04:40,717 --> 00:04:42,807
关键是想象两个世界
The key move is to imagine two worlds.

82
00:04:43,127 --> 00:04:44,983
一边是数据库 x
In one, the database is x.

83
00:04:45,303 --> 00:04:48,951
另一边是 x′：只有一条记录不同
In the other, it is x′: identical except for one row.

84
00:04:49,271 --> 00:04:50,587
比如 Alice 那条
Say, Alice's.

85
00:04:50,637 --> 00:04:52,962
这样的一对叫相邻数据库（也叫相邻数据集）
Databases like this are called neighbors.

86
00:04:53,282 --> 00:04:57,741
医院例子里多了 Alice；这里是她的记录变了
In the hospital, Alice was added; here, her row just says something different.

87
00:04:58,061 --> 00:05:01,048
总之，谁的记录都不该影响太大
Either way, no single person's row should matter much.

88
00:05:01,284 --> 00:05:05,934
运行这个机制，也就是数据管理者随机作答的规则，两个世界各一次
Run the mechanism, the curator's randomized answering rule, in each world.

89
00:05:06,254 --> 00:05:10,371
分析者能看到的一切，原文叫 transcript（交互历史）
Whatever the analyst gets to see, the paper calls the transcript;

90
00:05:10,371 --> 00:05:12,334
目前就是一个带噪声的答案
for now, a single noisy answer.

91
00:05:12,654 --> 00:05:14,588
因为机制是随机的
Because the mechanism is random,

92
00:05:14,588 --> 00:05:18,094
每个世界都给出一整个输出分布
each world gives a whole distribution of possible outputs.

93
00:05:18,334 --> 00:05:21,811
任取一个输出 t，比较两条曲线在这里的高度
Pick any output t, and compare the heights of the two curves there.

94
00:05:22,131 --> 00:05:24,478
滑动 t，看它们的比值
Slide t along and watch their ratio.

95
00:05:24,798 --> 00:05:30,243
满足差分隐私的机制，让比值处处接近 1
A private mechanism keeps that ratio close to 1 everywhere:

96
00:05:30,243 --> 00:05:33,566
不超过 e^ε，也不低于 e^(−ε)
never above e^ε, never below e^(−ε).

97
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:38,493
这就是原文的定义，叫作 ε-不可区分性（即 ε-差分隐私）
That is the paper's definition, which it calls ε-indistinguishability.

98
00:05:38,813 --> 00:05:41,800
比值的对数，就是 t 处的隐私损失
The log of the ratio is the privacy loss at t.

99
00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:46,179
对任意一对相邻数据库、任意分析者
For every pair of neighbors, every analyst and every output,

100
00:05:46,179 --> 00:05:48,818
任意输出，它的绝对值都不能超过 ε
it must be at most ε in absolute value.

101
00:05:49,138 --> 00:05:54,984
取绝对值就对称了：比值是 2 还是 1/2，都算一样
The absolute value makes it symmetric: a ratio of 2 and a ratio of 1/2 count the same.

102
00:05:55,304 --> 00:05:59,592
ε 很小的时候，e^ε 约等于 1 + ε
For small ε, e^ε is about 1 + ε.

103
00:05:59,834 --> 00:06:02,074
拿地图上 Warner 的硬币试试
Let's test it on Warner's coin from our map.

104
00:06:02,394 --> 00:06:05,466
暂停想一想：如果 Alice 的真实答案为“是”
Pause and ponder: if Alice's true answer is yes,

105
00:06:05,466 --> 00:06:07,322
她有多大概率说“是”？
how likely is she to say yes?

106
00:06:07,642 --> 00:06:09,242
换成“否”呢？
And if it is no?

107
00:06:21,567 --> 00:06:26,687
真实答案为“是”，她说“是”的概率是 3/4：正面，或者先反后正
If the truth is yes, she says yes 3/4 of the time: heads, or tails then heads.

108
00:06:27,007 --> 00:06:30,783
换成“否”，只有第二枚硬币能让她说“是”：1/4
If it is no, only the second coin can say yes: 1/4.

109
00:06:31,103 --> 00:06:35,092
最坏的比值是 3，所以硬币满足定义
The worst ratio is 3, so the coin satisfies the definition with ε = ln 3, about 1.1.

110
00:06:35,092 --> 00:06:39,082
ε 就等于 3 的对数，大约 1.1
The worst ratio is 3, so the coin satisfies the definition with ε = ln 3, about 1.1.

111
00:06:39,317 --> 00:06:42,474
现在你是攻击者，想区分这两个世界
Now be the attacker, trying to tell the two worlds apart.

112
00:06:42,794 --> 00:06:47,701
按贝叶斯公式，后验概率比恰好是先验概率比乘这个比值
By Bayes' rule, your new odds are your old odds times exactly this ratio,

113
00:06:47,701 --> 00:06:52,138
所以变化倍数最多是 e^ε，无论你之前知道什么
so they move by at most a factor of e^ε, whatever you knew before.

114
00:06:52,458 --> 00:06:54,586
从五五开出发，ε 取 0.1
Starting from 50/50,

115
00:06:54,586 --> 00:07:00,757
最多有 52.5% 的把握；取 1，最多 73%
ε = 0.1 leaves you at most 52.5% sure; ε = 1, at most 73%.

116
00:07:01,077 --> 00:07:04,618
ε 是人为选定的；原文管它叫 leakage（泄露量）
ε is set by policy; the paper calls it the leakage.

117
00:07:04,867 --> 00:07:06,723
再来看它不保证什么
Notice what this does not promise.

118
00:07:07,043 --> 00:07:10,300
假如研究发现吸烟者更容易得心脏病
If a study reveals that smokers get more heart disease,

119
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:13,912
而 Alice 吸烟，别人现在就可能觉得她风险更高
and Alice smokes, people may now think she is at higher risk.

120
00:07:14,232 --> 00:07:18,843
这不算侵犯隐私：同样的结论从其他人的数据里也能得出
That is not a privacy violation: the same lesson could be learned from everyone

121
00:07:18,843 --> 00:07:23,747
所以就算把 Alice 的记录换成别人的，也照样会发生
else's data, so it would happen even if Alice's row were replaced by someone else's.

122
00:07:25,183 --> 00:07:28,149
为什么每个输出的比值都要有上界？
Why demand a ratio bound for every single output?

123
00:07:28,469 --> 00:07:31,407
密码学常常满足于更弱的东西
Cryptography often settles for something weaker:

124
00:07:31,407 --> 00:07:35,018
统计距离（即 TV 距离），也就是两条曲线间面积的一半
statistical distance, half the area between the two curves.

125
00:07:35,338 --> 00:07:39,903
等价地说，就是任意事件的概率在两个世界间的最大差距
Equivalently, the most the probability of any event can differ between the worlds.

126
00:07:40,223 --> 00:07:42,612
原文说明了它在这里为什么不够
The paper shows why that is not enough here.

127
00:07:42,850 --> 00:07:47,672
看这个机制：随机挑一条记录，原样发布
Consider this mechanism: pick one row at random and publish it, word for word.

128
00:07:47,992 --> 00:07:53,048
改动一个人的记录，输出分布只会变化 1/n
Change one person's row, and the output distribution moves by only 1/n.

129
00:07:53,368 --> 00:07:55,197
数据库很大时这点变化微不足道
For a big database that is tiny,

130
00:07:55,197 --> 00:07:57,826
所以按平均来衡量，它看起来不泄露隐私
so by the averaged measure this looks private.

131
00:07:58,066 --> 00:08:00,605
可每个输出都是某个人的完整记录
But every output is somebody's complete record.

132
00:08:00,925 --> 00:08:05,971
比值这一关能拦住它：显示 Alice 真实取值的输出
The ratio test catches it: the output showing Alice's real value has

133
00:08:05,971 --> 00:08:09,608
一个世界里概率是 1/n，另一个是 0
probability 1/n in one world, and 0 in the other.

134
00:08:09,928 --> 00:08:11,528
比值是无穷大
The ratio is infinite.

135
00:08:11,666 --> 00:08:16,744
平均值会放过灾难，只要每场灾难对每个人都很罕见
Averages let catastrophes slip through, as long as each is rare for any single person.

136
00:08:17,064 --> 00:08:19,560
而比值上界会处处把它们排除在外
A ratio bound rules them out everywhere.

137
00:08:19,880 --> 00:08:23,169
它也解答了四舍五入那道题：在跳变处
It also settles our rounding question: at the jump,

138
00:08:23,169 --> 00:08:28,136
一个世界给出这个答案的概率是 1，另一个是 0
one world gives that answer with probability 1, the other with probability 0.

139
00:08:28,456 --> 00:08:31,442
想过这一关，机制就必须是随机的
To pass this test, a mechanism has to be random.

140
00:08:32,883 --> 00:08:34,547
那噪声到底要加多少？
So how much noise do we need?

141
00:08:34,867 --> 00:08:38,869
这只取决于 query 的一个性质：它的敏感度
It depends on a single property of the query: its sensitivity,

142
00:08:38,869 --> 00:08:42,612
也就是改变一条记录最多能让答案变化多少
the most that changing one row can ever change the answer,

143
00:08:42,612 --> 00:08:47,646
取遍每一对相邻数据库，包括还不存在的那些
over all pairs of neighboring databases, including ones that do not exist yet.

144
00:08:47,883 --> 00:08:50,725
对 counting query（计数查询）
For a counting query, like our hospital count,

145
00:08:50,725 --> 00:08:53,195
比如医院那个，一条记录最多让答案变 1
one row changes the answer by at most 1.

146
00:08:53,515 --> 00:08:54,950
敏感度是 1
Sensitivity 1.

147
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:59,163
再看直方图：把一条记录的可能取值分成 d 个桶
Now a histogram: split the possible values of a row into d bins,

148
00:08:59,163 --> 00:09:01,699
发布每个桶的记录数
and release how many rows fall in each.

149
00:09:02,019 --> 00:09:03,586
先别急着看答案，暂停一下
Before I show you, pause:

150
00:09:03,586 --> 00:09:08,163
如果 Alice 的记录变了，整个直方图总共能变多少？
if Alice's row changes, how much can the whole histogram change in total?

151
00:09:08,483 --> 00:09:10,338
这和桶的数量有关吗？
Does it depend on the number of bins?

152
00:09:19,183 --> 00:09:21,992
她从一个桶搬到另一个桶
She moves out of one bin and into another:

153
00:09:21,992 --> 00:09:25,135
一个桶少了 1，另一个桶多了 1
one count goes down by 1, another goes up by 1.

154
00:09:25,455 --> 00:09:27,055
总变化量：2
Total change: 2.

155
00:09:27,183 --> 00:09:31,646
像这样把各个分量变化的绝对值加起来
Adding up absolute changes across coordinates like this is the L1 norm,

156
00:09:31,646 --> 00:09:35,418
就是 L1 范数，原文就用它来衡量一列数的敏感度
the paper's way to measure sensitivity for lists of numbers.

157
00:09:35,738 --> 00:09:39,023
而且它总是 2，不管是 5 个桶还是 5000 个桶
And it is 2 whether there are 5 bins or 5000.

158
00:09:39,343 --> 00:09:41,540
它和维度完全无关
It does not depend on the dimension at all.

159
00:09:41,783 --> 00:09:45,602
对比一下：数据库里最高的收入是多少？
Contrast that with: what is the largest income in the database?

160
00:09:45,922 --> 00:09:46,987
一个亿万富翁
One billionaire can

161
00:09:46,987 --> 00:09:51,021
就能让答案变动 10 亿，不封顶就根本没有上限
move that answer by a billion, and with no cap there is no limit at all.

162
00:09:51,341 --> 00:09:55,095
标准做法是先给每个值封顶，比如 100 万
The standard fix is to cap every value, say at a million, first.

163
00:09:55,415 --> 00:09:59,895
这个 trick 要记住：差分隐私深度学习对梯度做的就是这个
Remember that trick: it is exactly what private deep learning does to gradients.

164
00:10:00,133 --> 00:10:01,726
有两点要记住
Two things to remember.

165
00:10:01,776 --> 00:10:04,866
敏感度只取决于函数本身
Sensitivity is a property of the function alone,

166
00:10:04,866 --> 00:10:08,923
与具体的数据库无关，也不是人为选定的
not of the particular database, and it is not chosen by policy.

167
00:10:09,243 --> 00:10:10,843
ε 是选择
ε is a choice.

168
00:10:10,971 --> 00:10:12,571
敏感度是事实
Sensitivity is a fact.

169
00:10:13,967 --> 00:10:15,325
下面来看噪声
Now for the noise.

170
00:10:15,375 --> 00:10:19,471
原文用的是拉普拉斯分布：左右对称
The paper uses the Laplace distribution: symmetric, sharply peaked,

171
00:10:19,471 --> 00:10:23,140
峰很尖，并且随着离中心的距离指数衰减
and falling off exponentially with distance from the center.

172
00:10:23,460 --> 00:10:26,106
它的宽度由尺度参数 λ 决定
Its width is set by a scale parameter, λ.

173
00:10:27,150 --> 00:10:28,508
关键的 trick 来了
Here is the trick.

174
00:10:28,558 --> 00:10:31,648
一条拉普拉斯曲线的中心在 f(x)，也就是 41
Center one Laplace curve at f(x), 41,

175
00:10:31,648 --> 00:10:37,412
另一条在 f(x′)，也就是 42：这就是两个世界的输出分布
and another at f(x′), 42: the output distributions of our two worlds.

176
00:10:37,650 --> 00:10:40,722
现在对每个输出 t，画出两条曲线比值的对数
Now plot the log of their ratio for every output t.

177
00:10:41,042 --> 00:10:43,858
在 41 左边，它完全是个常数
To the left of 41, it is exactly constant.

178
00:10:44,178 --> 00:10:46,460
在 42 右边，又是个常数
To the right of 42, constant again.

179
00:10:46,780 --> 00:10:48,402
中间是一段笔直的斜坡
In between, a straight ramp.

180
00:10:48,722 --> 00:10:56,168
它从不超过 1/λ，也从不低于 −1/λ：也就是平移量除以尺度
It never rises above 1/λ, and never falls below −1/λ: the shift, divided by the scale.

181
00:10:56,817 --> 00:10:57,769
为什么？
Why?

182
00:10:57,819 --> 00:11:00,827
取对数之后，拉普拉斯密度是个帐篷形
On a log scale, a Laplace density is a tent whose sides have slope 1/λ, never steeper.

183
00:11:00,827 --> 00:11:03,835
两边的斜率是 1/λ，绝不会更陡
On a log scale, a Laplace density is a tent whose sides have slope 1/λ, never steeper.

184
00:11:04,155 --> 00:11:07,083
把帐篷平移过去，两个帐篷的高度差
Slide the tent over, and the gap between the tents

185
00:11:07,083 --> 00:11:09,659
永远不超过平移量乘以这个斜率
can never exceed the slide times that slope.

186
00:11:09,979 --> 00:11:12,194
这就是整个设计原则
That is the whole design principle:

187
00:11:12,194 --> 00:11:15,548
隐私需要对数密度处处不陡的噪声
privacy needs noise whose log density is never steep.

188
00:11:16,284 --> 00:11:21,468
用符号写出来：到 t 的两段距离，最多相差两个中心之间的距离
In symbols: two distances to t can differ by at most the distance between the centers.

189
00:11:21,788 --> 00:11:26,609
所以任意输出的隐私损失，最多是敏感度除以 λ
So the privacy loss of any output is at most the sensitivity divided by λ.

190
00:11:26,929 --> 00:11:31,827
让 λ 取敏感度除以 ε，比值就始终在 e^ε 以内
Set λ to the sensitivity over ε, and the ratio stays within e^ε,

191
00:11:31,827 --> 00:11:35,270
对任意输出、任意一对相邻数据库都成立
for every output and every pair of neighbors.

192
00:11:35,590 --> 00:11:37,489
隐私，一个不等式就证完了
Privacy, proven in one line.

193
00:11:37,734 --> 00:11:42,427
如果 query 返回好几个数，就给每个数加上独立的拉普拉斯噪声
If the query returns several numbers, add independent Laplace noise to each.

194
00:11:42,747 --> 00:11:46,160
这时联合密度取决于 L1 距离
The joint density then depends on the L1 distance,

195
00:11:46,160 --> 00:11:50,256
正因为这样，敏感度才用 L1 范数来衡量
which is exactly why sensitivity is measured in the L1 norm.

196
00:11:50,576 --> 00:11:56,699
这就是命题 1：在每个分量上加尺度为 S(f)/ε 的拉普拉斯噪声
That is Proposition 1: Laplace noise of scale S(f)/ε in every coordinate.

197
00:11:56,934 --> 00:12:00,025
暂停想一想：为什么不用更简单的
Pause and ponder: why not something simpler,

198
00:12:00,025 --> 00:12:03,398
比如均匀噪声，−10 到 +10 之间任意取值？
like uniform noise anywhere between −10 and +10?

199
00:12:14,234 --> 00:12:15,613
看看边缘
Look at the edges.

200
00:12:15,663 --> 00:12:19,838
输出 51.5，真实人数是 42 就可能，是 41 就不可能
An output of 51.5 is possible if the true count is 42,

201
00:12:19,838 --> 00:12:26,564
又是那个无穷大比值，随机发布一条记录的机制当初就栽在这上面
but impossible if it is 41: the same infinite ratio that sank the random-row mechanism.

202
00:12:26,884 --> 00:12:29,167
好的噪声，绝不能把任何输出排除在外
Good noise must never rule an output out.

203
00:12:29,400 --> 00:12:31,320
那为什么不用熟悉的钟形曲线？
And why not the familiar bell curve?

204
00:12:31,640 --> 00:12:35,288
取对数之后，高斯是一条抛物线，越来越陡
On a log scale a Gaussian is a parabola, steeper and steeper,

205
00:12:35,288 --> 00:12:38,936
所以两条平移开的抛物线，高度差会无限增大
so the gap between two shifted parabolas grows without bound.

206
00:12:39,256 --> 00:12:43,117
到了尾部，比值会爆炸，没有哪个 ε 能管用
In the tails the ratio explodes, and no single ε works.

207
00:12:43,437 --> 00:12:46,243
不过先记住这个高斯：它还会回来
Hold on to that Gaussian, though: it comes back,

208
00:12:46,243 --> 00:12:50,862
用差分隐私训练神经网络时，实际用的就是它
and it is the noise you would actually use to train a neural network privately.

209
00:12:51,100 --> 00:12:57,094
这就是标题里的那条公式：噪声尺度等于敏感度除以 ε
So here is the recipe in the title: noise scale equals sensitivity divided by ε.

210
00:12:57,414 --> 00:12:59,974
敏感度越高的 query，噪声越大
A more sensitive question needs more noise.

211
00:13:00,294 --> 00:13:02,492
隐私越强，噪声越大
Stronger privacy needs more noise.

212
00:13:04,033 --> 00:13:08,471
回到医院的例子，ε 取 0.5：尺度为 2 的拉普拉斯噪声
Back to the hospital, with ε = 0.5: Laplace noise of scale 2.

213
00:13:08,791 --> 00:13:12,289
第一周，管理者报出大约 43.7
Week 1, the curator reports about 43.7.

214
00:13:12,609 --> 00:13:16,343
第二周，真实人数是 42，报出大约 40.6
Week 2, when the true count is 42, about 40.6.

215
00:13:16,663 --> 00:13:20,652
跟之前一样做减法，Alice 好像让人数少了 3
Subtract as before, and Alice seems to have lowered the count by 3.

216
00:13:20,972 --> 00:13:25,537
原本对她的判断是五五开，现在最多能有大约 62% 的把握
A 50/50 guess about her can now move to at most about 62%.

217
00:13:25,783 --> 00:13:30,114
再看噪声尺度取决于什么：敏感度和 ε
Now look at what the noise scale depends on: the sensitivity and ε.

218
00:13:30,434 --> 00:13:32,162
而不是数据库的规模
Not the size of the database.

219
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:37,800
有 100 个病人时，噪声一般在 2 左右，占答案的百分之几
With 100 patients, noise of typical size 2 is a few percent of the answer.

220
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:40,254
到了 100 万人，这点噪声可以忽略不计
With a million, it is a rounding error.

221
00:13:40,574 --> 00:13:45,424
保护 Alice 的噪声，比起她自己的贡献
Alice is protected by noise that is large compared to her own contribution,

222
00:13:45,424 --> 00:13:48,658
也就是 1，算是很大，但比起总体微不足道
which is 1, but tiny compared to the population's.

223
00:13:49,900 --> 00:13:51,522
隐私，留给个体
Privacy for individuals.

224
00:13:51,842 --> 00:13:53,612
准确，留给总体
Accuracy for populations.

225
00:13:53,932 --> 00:13:55,300
这就是差分隐私的取舍
That is the bargain.

226
00:13:55,350 --> 00:13:57,270
这一题你可以自己回答
Here is one you can answer yourself.

227
00:13:57,590 --> 00:14:01,409
暂停想一想：噪声大约有 1/ε 那么大
Pause and ponder: the noise has size about 1/ε.

228
00:14:01,729 --> 00:14:04,928
如果 ε 远小于 1/n，会出什么问题？
What goes wrong if ε is much smaller than 1/n?

229
00:14:17,766 --> 00:14:22,758
噪声超过了 n，比人数可能取到的任何值都大，答案成了纯噪声
The noise outgrows n, bigger than the count could ever be, and the answer is pure noise.

230
00:14:23,078 --> 00:14:24,828
这不是拉普拉斯噪声的问题
This is not Laplace's fault.

231
00:14:25,148 --> 00:14:30,817
任意两个数据库之间，都有一条最多 n 步的链
Any two databases are linked by a chain of at most n single-row changes,

232
00:14:30,817 --> 00:14:34,202
每步只改一条记录，概率之比最多是 e^ε
each changing probabilities by at most e^ε,

233
00:14:34,202 --> 00:14:37,116
所以两端之比最多是 e^(nε)
so the ends differ by at most e^(nε).

234
00:14:37,436 --> 00:14:42,214
如果 nε 极小，所有数据库看起来都一样，什么也学不到
If nε is tiny, every database looks alike, and nothing can be learned.

235
00:14:42,534 --> 00:14:45,025
这种链式 trick 叫 hybrid argument（混合论证）
This chain trick is called a hybrid argument,

236
00:14:45,025 --> 00:14:46,630
最后还会再出现
and it comes back at the end.
